Z||000005||Jncomutt||12-24-2001||01:00 PM||||You might also have air in your heater core.  Its basically a radiator.  If you get air bubbles in there, they almost never work themselves out and will decrease the heating effiency Greatly.  There are notes on 'burping' the heater core somewhere on the web. I can't remember where I read it.   Can anyone back me up on this???||||reg||1
